// ============================================================================
// dark_re_wilding — /rw_preview : the legend PUSH tier's delivery.
//
// STATUS: written 2026-09-25 by the bridge pass, UNVERIFIED — no engine was booted and no
// sclang was run. It is deliberately a SEPARATE, ADDITIVE file rather than an edit to
// sc/parse_dark_re_wilding.scd, so that nothing here can break the shipped engine's parse.
// Whoever owns the engine should either fold it into parse_dark_re_wilding.scd (it belongs
// after \rwPoint) or load it from sc/dark_re_wilding_boot.scd with one line:
//     (~projDir +/+ "rw_preview.scd").load;
// Load AFTER dark_re_wilding_synths.scd and parse_dark_re_wilding.scd — it reuses ~rwBody,
// ~rwBus, ~rwAlive, ~rwWatch, ~rwArpNodes, ~rwMix and the level constants from those.
//
// WHY IT EXISTS. /rw_point restarts the navigation timeline: it forces ~rwClaveOn = false
// and \claveAmp = 0, kills the arp nodes and the corpus, and only brings the clave back
// after ~rwClaveIn = 2.0 s, with the arp's first note at 2 + max(1.2, 2*barSched) =
// 3.2–5.2 s. Ten of the legend's fifteen rows are clave rows, so on the commit path a hold
// reads: tick → 2 s of silence → tick at the new rate → release → 2 s of silence → tick at
// the old rate. That is an A/B of two silences. The drone rows DO work on the commit path,
// because gains and combDecay are set before the Routine — which is the trap: a smoke test
// looks fine and the rows Miguel actually asked for are unusable.
//
// IT IS NOT A SECOND COOKING FUNCTION (manual C5 §19.2). The numbers arrive from the same
// tables through the same arithmetic on the bridge side; this is a second DELIVERY of the
// same state that does not restart a timeline. Keep the distinction in this comment or
// someone will "simplify" it back into \rwPoint.
//
// IT NEVER TOUCHES ~rwState, ~rwMix, ~rwSubset, ~rwLevel, the identity or the timeline.
// One variable of state is kept here and one only: ~rwPreviewClaveWas.
//
// LAYER ISOLATION (Miguel, 2026-09-25): "if i am changing values to hear the drone
// difference, dont play again the clave, just the drone. if i am changing values to hear the
// clave diff, just play the clave over the drone, and so on." A preview sounds the layer
// under test plus the layers beneath it AS A STILL BED - and the bed is composed on the
// bridge side, which already holds the listener's own payload. THE ONE CAPABILITY THIS FILE
// HAD TO GROW FOR IT IS A CLAVE MUTE, because measured live neither existing path can mute
// the tick without lying:
//   * /rw_mix clave=0 does mute it (claveAmp 0.0680 -> 0.0000, verified) but RW_MIX is the
//     LISTENER's mixer, broadcast to every page - a preview must not drag their fader.
//   * /rw_preview ["clave", r, f, a, 0] rewrites rate/formant/accent and LEAVES claveAmp:
//     measured, claveAmp stayed 0.0680 while the rate went 5.733 -> 2.0 and the accent 3 -> 7.
//     On a drone row that leaves the tick running AT THE PUSHED TEMPO - worse than today.
//   * sending nothing leaves a running tick running at the listener's rate: still audible,
//     still not the rule.
// Hence "claveoff", below, which sets \claveAmp 0 AND ~rwClaveOn = false. BOTH HALVES ARE
// LOAD-BEARING: OSCdef(\rwMix) writes claveAmp whenever ~rwClaveOn is true (verified live),
// so a fader touch mid-hold would otherwise un-mute the row.
//
// PROTOCOL
//   /rw_preview ["drone", theta, pressure, g0..g34]
//        theta is carried for the log line only; the body reads the gains and the pressure.
//   /rw_preview ["clave", rate, formant, accent, on]
//        `on` = 1 also forces the tick audible, because a listener who presses a clave chip
//        more than ~10.5 s after landing would otherwise hear nothing: the navigation
//        timeline has already stopped the tick on a downbeat.
//   /rw_preview ["claveoff"]
//        mute the tick for the length of the hold, recording what it found so that "end"
//        can put it back. A DISTINCT VERB, not "clave" with on=0, for two reasons: the
//        bridge's own restore re-sends a clave for any hold whose verbs contain "clave", and
//        a silent clave still has to carry rate/formant/accent it is not being given.
//   /rw_preview ["cert", c0, c1, ... cN]
//        instant, gapless, no respawn — the one arp change that is a steady-state property
//        of a ringing note. Applied in spawn order over the preview nodes if any, else over
//        the listener's own; a short list reuses its last value.
//   /rw_preview ["chord", gap, n, f,a,c, f,a,c, ...]
//        a preview chord that SUSTAINS until "end" — a hold is held, so there is no
//        ~rwArpSustain timeout. \maxDur stays as the orphan backstop; it already saved a
//        live server once (37 stuck voices, 2026-09-23).
//   /rw_preview ["end"]
//        stop and gate off the preview chord; put the clave back the way it was found.
//        IT DOES NOT RESTORE THE DRONE OR THE CLAVE PARAMETERS — the bridge re-sends the
//        listener's own values as ordinary previews immediately before it, because the
//        bridge already holds them. Duplicating that state here is how two copies drift.
//
// DONE IN parse_dark_re_wilding.scd (line 265): ~rwPreviewClear.value is called at the top of
// OSCdef(\rwPoint), so navigating while a chip is held cannot leave a preview chord, a forced
// clave or - now - a MUTED one behind. The bridge already sends ["end"] before every commit,
// so it is belt-and-braces rather than load-bearing; a page that dies mid-hold sends nothing,
// which is the case it is there for. The order matters and is right: the clear restores the
// tick, and the commit's own `~rwClaveOn = false; claveAmp 0` two lines later re-silences it
// for the new point, so a mute can never outlive the hold that made it.
// ============================================================================
(
~rwPreviewArpNodes = ~rwPreviewArpNodes ? List.new;
~rwPreviewRoutine  = ~rwPreviewRoutine;
// nil = no clave preview has happened in this hold. false / true = what ~rwClaveOn was when
// the hold's first clave preview arrived - whether that was a "clave" that forced the tick ON
// or a "claveoff" that muted it. THE ONLY STATE THIS FILE KEEPS, and it is now read in both
// directions: the release puts the tick back to what the hold FOUND, rather than only
// undoing a forced ON. A hold that never touched the clave leaves it nil and is not restored.
~rwPreviewClaveWas = ~rwPreviewClaveWas;

// drop dead preview references the same way \rwArpNodes does, so the list cannot grow
~rwPreviewEnded.notNil.if { ~rwPreviewEnded.free };
~rwPreviewEnded = OSCFunc({ |msg|
    var id = msg[1];
    ~rwPreviewArpNodes.notNil.if {
        ~rwPreviewArpNodes = List.newFrom(~rwPreviewArpNodes.reject { |nd| nd.nodeID == id }) };
}, '/n_end', s.addr);

~rwPreviewClear = {
    ~rwPreviewRoutine.notNil.if { ~rwPreviewRoutine.stop; ~rwPreviewRoutine = nil };
    ~rwPreviewArpNodes.do { |nd| ~rwAlive.value(nd).if { nd.set(\gate, 0) } };
    ~rwPreviewArpNodes = List.new;
    ~rwPreviewChordOn = false;          // the navigation chord may spawn again (P38)
    // PUT THE TICK BACK THE WAY THE HOLD FOUND IT. `nil` means no clave preview happened in
    // this hold, and a hold that never touched the clave must not turn it either way.
    //   false -> it was off. Either the hold forced it on (a clave or arp row) or it muted a
    //            tick that was already silent (a drone row pressed after the timeline's
    //            downbeat stop, where the mute was a no-op): both restore to off.
    //   true  -> it was on. Either the hold muted it (a drone row) or it re-stated it (a
    //            clave or arp row, where reviving is a no-op): both restore to on.
    // THE ONE RACE, and it is why this is not just `~rwClaveOn = ~rwPreviewClaveWas`: the
    // navigation timeline stops the tick on a downbeat ~10.4 s after a point, which can fall
    // INSIDE a hold. Reviving then would turn on a tick the timeline had just retired. That
    // stop is the LAST STATEMENT of ~rwRoutine, so a timeline still suspended on a wait has
    // not reached it yet. MEASURED in sclang 3.13.0 rather than assumed: a Routine suspended
    // on a SystemClock wait reads state 5 / isPlaying true, one that has run to the end of
    // its function reads 6 / false, and one that has been .play'd but not yet reached its
    // first tick reads 0 / false. That last case cannot reach this line: it is only consulted
    // when the tick was FOUND ON, and the tick only becomes audible ~rwClaveIn = 2.0 s into
    // the timeline, by which point the routine is long since suspended.
    ~rwPreviewClaveWas.notNil.if {
        (~rwPreviewClaveWas and: { ~rwRoutine.notNil } and: { ~rwRoutine.isPlaying }).if({
            ~rwAlive.value(~rwBody).if {
                ~rwBody.set(\claveAmp, ~rwClaveLevel * ~rwMix[\clave]) };
            ~rwClaveOn = true;
        }, {
            ~rwAlive.value(~rwBody).if { ~rwBody.set(\claveAmp, 0) };
            ~rwClaveOn = false;
        });
    };
    ~rwPreviewClaveWas = nil;
};

OSCdef(\rwPreview, { |msg|
    var verb = msg[1].asString, maxModes = 35;
    case
    { verb == "drone" } {
        var gains = Array.fill(maxModes, { |i|
            ((4 + i) < msg.size).if({ msg[4 + i].asFloat }, { 0 }) });
        ~rwAlive.value(~rwBody).if {
            ~rwBody.setn(\gains, gains);
            ~rwBody.set(\combDecay, 0.10 + (0.45 * msg[3].asFloat.clip(0, 1)));
        };
    }
    { verb == "clave" } {
        // SAVE ON THE FIRST CLAVE PREVIEW OF A HOLD, not on every one: the bridge sends a
        // clave with every drone-or-clave preview, and re-saving would record "on" the
        // second time round and leave the tick running after the finger lifted.
        ~rwPreviewClaveWas.isNil.if { ~rwPreviewClaveWas = ~rwClaveOn };
        ~rwAlive.value(~rwBody).if {
            ~rwBody.set(\claveRate, msg[2].asFloat.max(0.1),
                        \claveFormant, msg[3].asFloat,
                        \claveAccent, msg[4].asInteger.max(1));
            (msg[5].asInteger == 1).if {
                ~rwBody.set(\claveAmp, ~rwClaveLevel * ~rwMix[\clave]);
                ~rwClaveOn = true;
            };
        };
    }
    { verb == "claveoff" } {
        // THE LAYER-ISOLATION MUTE. It RECORDS what it found rather than assuming the tick
        // was running: a clave the navigation timeline has already stopped is ~rwClaveOn
        // false with claveAmp already 0, so the mute is a no-op AND the release must not
        // turn it on. Saved on the FIRST clave-touching verb of a hold only, exactly as the
        // "clave" branch does, so a second preview inside the same hold cannot overwrite it.
        ~rwPreviewClaveWas.isNil.if { ~rwPreviewClaveWas = ~rwClaveOn };
        ~rwAlive.value(~rwBody).if { ~rwBody.set(\claveAmp, 0) };
        ~rwClaveOn = false;
    }
    { verb == "cert" } {
        var vals = msg.copyToEnd(2).collect(_.asFloat);
        var nodes = (~rwPreviewArpNodes.size > 0).if({ ~rwPreviewArpNodes }, { ~rwArpNodes });
        (vals.size > 0).if {
            nodes.do { |nd, i|
                ~rwAlive.value(nd).if { nd.set(\cert, vals[i.min(vals.size - 1)]) };
            };
        };
    }
    { verb == "chord" } {
        var gap = msg[2].asFloat.max(0.02), n = msg[3].asInteger;
        var notes = Array.fill(n, { |i|
            [msg[4 + (3 * i)].asFloat, msg[5 + (3 * i)].asFloat, msg[6 + (3 * i)].asFloat] });
        // the listener's own chord goes quiet too: a preview is an A/B of ONE chord - and it
        // STAYS quiet: while this is held the navigation routine spawns none of its remaining
        // notes, and if it had already begun, none of them this commit (TASKS P38; the note
        // loop in parse_dark_re_wilding.scd \rwPoint reads both flags)
        (~rwArpNodes.size > 0).if { ~rwArpCut = true };
        ~rwPreviewChordOn = true;
        ~rwPreviewRoutine.notNil.if { ~rwPreviewRoutine.stop; ~rwPreviewRoutine = nil };
        ~rwPreviewArpNodes.do { |nd| ~rwAlive.value(nd).if { nd.set(\gate, 0) } };
        ~rwPreviewArpNodes = List.new;
        ~rwArpNodes.do { |nd| ~rwAlive.value(nd).if { nd.set(\gate, 0) } };
        ~rwArpNodes = List.new;
        ~rwPreviewRoutine = Routine({
            notes.do { |nt, i|
                (i > 0).if { gap.wait };
                ~rwPreviewArpNodes.add(~rwWatch.value(
                    Synth(\rwArp, [\out, ~rwBus, \freq, nt[0], \amp, nt[1],
                                   \cert, nt[2], \rel, ~rwArpRelease,
                                   \arpGain, ~rwArpLevel * ~rwMix[\arp]])));
            };
            // NO ~rwArpSustain WAIT. A hold is held: the chord sustains until "end".
        }).play(SystemClock);
    }
    { verb == "end" } { ~rwPreviewClear.value }
    { true } { ("[rw] /rw_preview: unknown verb " ++ verb).postln };
}, '/rw_preview');

"[rw] /rw_preview ready: drone | clave | claveoff | cert | chord | end".postln;
)
